  "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\text{Null}(B)$ contains all vectors that, when pre-multiplied by $B,$ result in the zero-vector $0.$ \n\nWhen pre-multiplying a vector by $B,$ we actually multiply each row of $B$ by that vector. So, $\\text{Null}(B)$ must be orthogonal to the row space of $B,$ which is $\\text{Col}({A}^{T}).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"\n\n**Note:** In general, the four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $B$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14247906/assets/18713ed3d103ca0a02d74cede1e6448012e0aa28a2df804d41cfb277589a0158.png)",
